{"name": "Athletic", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can accomplish impressive feats of physical endurance. You gain proficiency in Strength (Athletics).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "2nd level overall and have at least one level in a Martial class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "VXLO74M9FQ5TRHU8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Going All-Out", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/unholy/strike-body-life-soul-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>After taking a desperate action, you can choose to act normally on your next turn, but cannot take desperate actions until then. Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "2nd level overall and have at least one level in a Martial class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "KHXTYYWW0CRFP2RN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sprinter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your base walking speed increases by 10 feet, and attacks of opportunity against you have disadvantage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "2nd level overall and have at least one level in a Martial class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "GOP7M90B2MXBCL8K", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Stalwart Physique", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/wounds/injury-body-pain-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can use Constitution in place of Dexterity when determining your AC. While you aren't wearing any armor, your AC is 12 + Your Dexterity or Constitution Modifier.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "2nd level overall and have at least one level in a Martial class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "17YBBWEXS5QW6W94", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tireless", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/day-night-sunset-sunrise.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Unlock: </em>When you reach 6th level overall you may take the ability below.</p><p>When you have @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion}, you suffer its effects as if you had half as many levels of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} (rounded down). Whenever you remove @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} as part of a long rest, you can remove an additional level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "2nd level overall and have at least one level in a Martial class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "MCOVKJ7UZMJQGXIQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Backing Artist", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/bust-carved-stone.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Harmonize with me.</em></p><p>Each time you take the <strong>Assist</strong> action, you can choose two of the following additional effects:</p><ul><li>The creature you assist becomes @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Choose a target within 60ft that can hear you to become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} until the end of your next turn. Instead of gaining advantage on their next check, the assisted creature has advantage on their next attack against this target.</li><li>The creature you assist can immediately take a minor action.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "XVWY4BL8VIERNETM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Timely Backup", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/hourglass-tilted-glowing-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a desperate action, you can move to any creature that is no more than half your movement speed away from you and use the <strong>Assist</strong> action on it. Unlike other desperate actions, you can use this ability to interrupt the desperate actions of willing creatures.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have a Bard Adept Ability", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "0QAS4D8W7N209D20", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Favorite Trope", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/scribal/ink-quill-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>A reliable component you can count on to grab an audience&rsquo;s interest.</em></p><p>The following is a list of familiar tropes that might emerge in your art. When you take this ability, choose one of the following tropes, as well as the trait with it.</p><p>Switching your favorite trope from one to another requires extensive rewrites, and can only be undertaken as part of the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.rest-actions.AZTVZVCUEPFQB5RN]{Prepare New Material} long rest action (See Bard&rsquo;s Spellcasting ability). If you choose to, you lose access to the trait of your previous Favorite Trope and may choose a different one.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Rivalry</strong></p><p><em>Nothing pushes people to perform at their best like a little friendly competition.</em></p><p><em>Trait:</em> Whenever you cause a creature to become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized}, you become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} yourself for the same duration and choose a second Attribute. Both of you can apply the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} bonus to both of the attributes that were chosen.</p><p><strong>Villain of the Week</strong></p><p><em>Villains are a silver piece a dozen. Strike one down, and another will step into their boots before the body&rsquo;s even gone cold.&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>Trait:</em> When a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} creature within 60ft of you is reduced to 0 hit points or killed, your first use of the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.018XFM2VDH6HIHL0]{Vilify} minor action within the next minute costs 0 Immersion. When this occurs, you can immediately take the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.018XFM2VDH6HIHL0]{Vilify} minor action as a reaction.</p><p><strong>Plot Armor</strong></p><p><em>It&rsquo;s not enough to single out a hero, they need to be made larger than life so that all who would stand against them are plagued by doubt that they could ever prevail.</em></p><p><em>Trait:</em> When a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} creature within 30ft of you is hit with an attack, you can use your reaction to increase their AC by one roll of the lionized die for that attack, potentially causing it to miss.</p><p>Additionally, when a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} creature within 30ft of you hits a creature with an attack, you can use your reaction to reduce the attack&rsquo;s damage by a roll of the villainized die.</p><p>You can activate both of these effects as a single reaction if the attacker is @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} and the target of the attack is @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "novice"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "O9XP2FKIHU39PPPC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Immersion", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Their eyes and ears may find the fictions, but the truth shall find their hearts.</em></p><p>Immersion is the subtle interpersonal power that a Bard taps into, a collective unspoken desire for drama and wonder that blurs the lines between the believable and the unbelievable. You as a Bard have the power to shepherd truths across this gap between expectation and reality, but only so long as you use it sparingly. After all, the last thing you want is to stretch believability so far that you break your audience&rsquo;s immersion.</p><p>This potential is represented by your Immersion, which you can spend to fuel various Bard abilities. Your maximum Immersion is 2 at 1st level. The maximum increases for every odd-numbered Bard level gained, starting at Bard level 3. For example, at Bard level 8, you can hold a maximum of 5 Immersion. If you would gain Immersion while already at your maximum you become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} for 10 minutes instead.</p><p>You regain all expended Immersion when you finish a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Immersive Storyteller", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-open-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>When you cause a creature to become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized}, the bonus die increases to 1d6 until they are no longer @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized}.</li><li>When you cause a creature to become @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized}, the damage die increases to 1d10 until they are no longer @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized}.</li><li>You gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{Immersion} when you roll Initiative.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "0U3IYHVQDRO4RJXM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Limelight", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/light/beam-strike-village-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>All the world is your stage, and your fellows and foes its stars. They may not know yet what parts they&rsquo;ll play, but come time for the curtains to fall you will have shown them.</em></p><p>While you are within 60 feet of a creature that can hear you, you can target it with the following abilities:</p><p><br /><strong>Glorify</strong></p><p><em>Talking up their achievements or potential, you give your ally a much needed confidence boost.</em></p><p>Spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{Immersion} as a minor action, the target becomes @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{Lionized} for 10 minutes.</p><p><br /><strong>Vilify</strong></p><p><em>Singling out a foe, you confront them on their foul deeds or harp on the flaw that will become their downfall.</em></p><p>Spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{Immersion} as a minor action, the target becomes @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} for 1 minute.</p><p><br /><strong>Catharsis</strong></p><p><em>The audience delights in seeing a villain getting what they deserve. Let them savor the moment a little longer.</em></p><p>As a reaction to a creature taking damage from the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{Villainized} condition, immediately restore its ability to take damage from the condition.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "018XFM2VDH6HIHL0", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Promoter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can spend a minor action to <strong>Assist</strong> a creature. Additionally, you can choose to @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.018XFM2VDH6HIHL0]{Glorify} or @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.018XFM2VDH6HIHL0]{Vilify} a creature as part of the same minor action, paying the usual cost.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "adept"}, "requirements": "6th level overall and 3rd level Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "FHJRNZE4BO3NRACH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spellcasting (Bard)", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-black-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As one who uses arcane means to bend this world to your will with magic, you have in your possession a spell book, or grimoire if you will.  And it is the guidebook to reconstructing your reality.</p><h4><strong>Cantrips</strong></h4><p>Upon gaining your 1st level of Bard, you know two Cantrips from the Bard&rsquo;s spell list.  You will learn additional Cantrips as you advance in the Bard class.  You gain an additional Cantrip when you hit Adept Bard, and then another at Expert Bard.</p><h4><strong>Spells at 1st Level</strong></h4><p>A Bard at 1st level knows four level 1 spells of their choice from the Bard&rsquo;s spell list.</p><h4><strong>Casting Spells</strong></h4><p>A Bard, like all spellcasters, expends Mana to cast spells (expanded upon in the Mana section of <strong>&ldquo;Chapter 9: Magic & Spellcasting&rdquo;</strong>).  As well, you regain your Mana fully on a long rest, and partially on a short rest.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You can cast any Bard spells you have learned.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(Note: To figure out how many and what spells you know, reference the <b>Spells at 1st Level</b> above this section, and if needed, the <b>Learning Spells at Higher Levels</b> section in the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.classes.MGOXKZCFR46MSF08]{Bard} Class.)</p><h4><strong>Spellcasting Ability</strong></h4><p>Given that your magic is brought to life through rousing performances, Presence is the spellcasting ability for a Bard.  This means that your Presence modifier comes into play when setting the DC for your Bard spells and when making an attack with one.</p><ul><li><i>Spell Save DC:</i> 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Presence modifier</li><li><i>Spell Attack Modifier:</i> your proficiency bonus + your Presence modifier</li></ul><h4><strong>Ritual Casting</strong></h4><p>You can cast a Bard spell as a Ritual if that spell has the Ritual tag and you have learned the spell.</p><h4><strong>Spellcasting Focus</strong></h4><p>You may use an arcane focus, a specialized item used for casting, as a spellcasting focus for casting your Bard spells, or a musical instrument you are proficient with.  Spellcasting focuses allow spells to be cast without needing the material components, but does not replace material components that have a cost or are said to be used up by the spell.</p><h4><strong>Prepare New Material</strong></h4><p>As a long rest action, you can choose to either replace one Bard cantrip you know with a different cantrip from the Bard spell list, or replace two Bard spells you know with two other spells from the Bard spell list that are of a level you can cast. @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.rest-actions.AZTVZVCUEPFQB5RN]{Prepare New Material}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ZD6YNR1QX0H3BJPP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bard Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-runed-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>1st level Bards get access to Bardic Magic, which consists of 1st through 7th level spells.  However, you do not have access to all of them right away.  These spell levels become accessible as follows:</p><p><i>Bard Spell Levels</i></p><table><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Unlock Requirements</th></tr><tr><td>Level 1 Spells</td><td>1st Level Bard.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 2 Spells</td><td>2nd Level Bard;<br>3rd Level Overall.</td></tr><tr><td>Level 3 Spells</td><td>3rd Level Bard;<br>5th Level Overall<br>(At least 4 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 4 Spells</td><td>4th Level Bard;<br>7th Level Overall<br>(At least 6 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 5 Spells</td><td>5th Level Bard;<br>9th Level Overall<br>(At least 8 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 6 Spells</td><td>6th Level Bard;<br>11th Level Overall<br>(At least 10 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr><tr><td>Level 7 Spells</td><td>7th Level Bard;<br>13th Level Overall<br>(At least 12 of these levels must be in Spellcaster classes).</td></tr></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "Bard", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "XTPYQVEB8Y00E344", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bloopers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/time/arrows-circling-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Whenever you witness a creature within 30 feet of you that is @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{&#x1F981; Lionized} fail an attack roll or check, you can use your reaction to make it roll again. On a success, it succeeds in its goal thanks to sheer luck, an improbable coincidence, or some other comically convoluted means.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once you cause a creature to succeed using this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a rest or unless you spend a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point as part of the reaction. The @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point is refunded if the creature fails the reroll.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "YNYRG1OSHNZ1HDC1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "People Person", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When trying to get a laugh out of a crowd, you've found it helps to know a bit about their experiences and values. You gain proficiency in Intelligence (Culture).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "UT2MT6HXQ4PUJKCF", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Prop Weapons", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/cooking/fork-steel-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your unexpected and exaggerated style of combat often catches opponents off guard. You are proficient with improvised weapons. Whenever you make an improvised weapon attack, you can use your Presence modifier in place of Strength or Dexterity for the attack and damage roll. When determining the damage of an improvised weapon, you can use 1d6 in place of its normal damage die, or 1d8 if you hold the object with two hands. If an improvised weapon you are wielding breaks as a result of hitting a creature, the attack deals an additional 1d4 damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "TJ4VKZYFH31W9X3V", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Self-Insert", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You're no stranger to physical forms of comedy, and know how best to play up a tumble to elicit concerned gasps and relieved laughs from your audience and even yourself, manifesting this internal comedic logic to shield you from the worst of it. Whenever you use a desperate action <b>Saving a Target</b> to comically get in the way of the attack, you have resistance to the attack's damage.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the damage you suffer (after any reductions) equal or exceeds your character level, gain a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "7RD3VKTZ5NAWVBRS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Slapstick", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/wood/furniture-stool-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Any time you would make a melee weapon attack, you can replace it with an attempt to <strong>Shove</strong> or <strong>Trip</strong> a target, not just when taking the Attack action. While you have a free hand, you can use your minor action to <strong>Shove</strong> or <strong>Trip</strong> a creature. Creatures you successfully <strong>Trip</strong> take 1d6 bludgeoning damage when they hit the ground.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Finally, when you are initiating or resisting an attempt to <strong>Shove</strong> or <strong>Trip</strong>, you can make a Presence (Perform) check in place of the normal check.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "OS4PU32OTOKG859U", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Theme: Levity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/mouth-smile-deception-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your art is fueled by the levity that comes with bewilderment, peculiarity, and irony. Whenever a creature that you can see within 60ft of you rolls a natural 1 on an attack roll or skill check, gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You can only benefit from one Theme ability at a time. If you have multiple Theme abilities, you can change which one is active when you finish a rest and any time you spend a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point on an ability.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "XS4831HQBSH7W2M4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Boarding Party", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/ship.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You&rsquo;re experienced at using ranged weaponry both at a distance and in the thick of a fray. Your ranged attacks no longer suffer disadvantage as a result of targeting a creature that is within 5 feet of you or prone.</p><p>Additionally, you can use your minor action to reload a weapon with the Loading property between attacks.</p><p>You learn the following Gambit: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.L65XCJ63D6V6QUVJ]{Gambit: Shot Across the Bow}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "W6WA5QK7MVTV83IS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Contingency Plan", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/navigation/map-marked-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Good luck only ever lasts so long. As a corsair, you&rsquo;re no stranger to cutthroats and thieves, and you&rsquo;re always waiting for the other boot to drop.&nbsp;</p><p>Whenever you are <strong>Surprised</strong>, you can still choose to do one of the following on your first turn of combat:</p><ul><li>Take an Action.</li><li>Move and take a Minor Action.</li><li>Gain temporary hit points equal to your level as a Non-Action.</li></ul><p>You also learn the following Gambits:&nbsp;@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.YUAJX59ZHM417PCB]{Gambit: Shake a Leg}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.150EJLYVPMDY2VLI]{Gambit: Loose Cannon}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "EW5EDFT4VENBU9QJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dead Men Tell No Tales", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-symbol-skull-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You&rsquo;re well-traveled and accustomed to conversing with parties on less than the most cooperative of terms. In that time you&rsquo;ve picked up a knack for &ldquo;putting things into perspective&rdquo;. You gain proficiency in Presence (Intimidation) or the Vehicle Trade.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "HLOE5LYM9Y1M9U58", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Avast, Me Hearties!", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Avast, Me Hearties!</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>As a minor action you can shout words of encouragement at a creature within 60 feet that can hear you. Spend one Panache dice to roll it and grant the creature temporary hit points equal to the number rolled.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "MQ87LWRH52O6XSGZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Loose Cannon", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Loose Cannon</strong></p><p><em>Cost: X Panache</em></p><p>Whenever you hit with an attack but are unable to use your Sneak Attack, you can choose to expend any number of Panache Dice to roll and add them to the attack&rsquo;s damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "150EJLYVPMDY2VLI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Scallywag", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Scallywag</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>When you make a Presence (Intimidation) or Presence (Deception) check but before learning whether you succeed or fail, you can expend a single Panache Die to roll it and add it to the result.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "Y26KXC52QC1Z8Z4L", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Getting Yer Sea Legs", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Getting Yer Sea Legs</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>When you make a check to climb or avoid being knocked @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone} but before learning whether you succeed or fail, you can expend a single Panache Die to roll it and add it to the result.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "0LCC8YZ2VZB77YR9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Shake a Leg", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Shake a Leg</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>Whenever you roll initiative and are not <strong>Surprised</strong>, you can expend a single Panache Die to roll it and add it to the result.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "YUAJX59ZHM417PCB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Shot Across the Bow", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Shot Across the Bow</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>When you miss a creature with a ranged attack that would have been eligible for Sneak Attack, you can expend your use of Sneak Attack this turn and one Panache Die to turn the attack into a warning shot. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom (Save) Check against your Sneak Attack DC or take psychic damage equal to a roll of the Panache Die and become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened} of you until the end of its next turn. A creature that would be reduced to 0 hit points by this damage faints instead, dropping to 1 hit point and falling @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious} for 1 minute.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "L65XCJ63D6V6QUVJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gambit: Weigh Anchor", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Gambit: Weigh Anchor</strong></p><p><em>Cost: 1 Panache</em></p><p>To use this gambit, you must be holding a rope with an attached grappling hook. As a minor action, or as part of the Dash action, you can expend one Panache Dice to secure the rope to any protrusion (such as a tree branch, rock outcropping, pole, or chandelier) at a distance of up to 30 feet from you and not exceeding the rope's length. You can alternatively attempt to secure it to a creature, however the creature can make a Dexterity (Save) Check versus your Sneak Attack DC to avoid it. A creature that can reach the hook can use their action to detach the grappling hook from the hooked target. You can use your action while touching a rope you secured with this ability to retrieve it and the attached grappling hook.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "OB8YW767NKUR0TXY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Panache", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/dice-pair-white-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a corsair, your effectiveness hinges upon taking bold risks to gain the upper hand. These feats of daring-do are represented by your Panache Dice, which are d6. You start with one Panache Die, and can hold up to a maximum of 1 + your Proficiency Bonus Panache Dice at a time. When you finish a long rest, you lose any unused Panache Dice and then gain one.</p><p>Gaining more Panache Dice to use requires taking risks. You can gain them in the following ways:</p><ul><li>Whenever you activate your Sneak Attack ability, you can choose to forgo up to half of your sneak attack dice in order to gain a Panache Die for each Sneak Attack die you sacrifice.</li><li>Before rolling a skill check you are proficient in for a non-trivial task, you can choose to take a penalty equal to your proficiency bonus in order to gain a Panache Die. This penalty is static and not increased by multipliers to your proficiency bonus, such as the Multi-Talented ability.</li></ul><p>You can use your Panache dice to fuel special abilities, called Corsair Gambits. You know one Gambit called <em>Scallywag</em>, detailed below, and can add new ones to your roster by taking the Corsair ability associated with each of them.</p><p><strong>Growth:</strong> Your Panache Die increases in size at each growth level, becoming a d8 at 5th level, d10 at 11th level, and d12 at 17th level.</p><p>You learn the following Gambit: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.Y26KXC52QC1Z8Z4L]{Gambit: Scallywag}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "EDSSCUMXYUHNCQ9F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Rakish Charm", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/materials/feather-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your daring and bombastic ploys have a penchant to amaze onlookers.</p><p>Once per turn, when you perform a Gambit you can force one creature that saw it to make a Wisdom (Save) Check versus your Sneak Attack DC. Creatures with an Intelligence score of less than 3 automatically succeed.</p><p>On a failed save, the creature is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by you until the end of its next turn. While a creature is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} in this way, its action can only be used to take the Disengage, Self-Defense, or Hide action. Once you charm a creature with this ability, that creature can&rsquo;t be @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by it again until you finish a long rest.</p><p>Whenever a creature fails its save against this ability, regardless of whether it can be @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} or not, you gain advantage on the first Presence check directed at it within the next minute.</p><p>You also learn the following Gambit: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.MQ87LWRH52O6XSGZ]{Gambit: Avast, Me Hearties!}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "LYCMR7TCA8JCT44F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Rigged Fight", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/nautical/rope-line-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are adept at climbing and swinging from ropes whilst in the thick of combat. Once per turn, immediately after swinging at least 10 feet on a rope or chain, your first weapon attack against a target that is within 5 feet of you gains advantage.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Additionally, you can climb ropes and chains at your normal walking speed and can perform Long Jumps off of them as handily as from the ground (Refer to &lsquo;Jumping&rsquo; in <strong>&ldquo;Chapter 7: Combat&rdquo;</strong>). Each turn, the first 10 feet of horizontal movement you make while swinging costs you no movement.</p><p>You also learn the following Gambits:&nbsp;@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.OB8YW767NKUR0TXY]{Gambit: Weigh Anchor}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.0LCC8YZ2VZB77YR9]{Gambit: Getting Yer Sea Legs}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Have the Rogue Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "OVP7QML1V8RHMWEZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hungering Shadows", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/wolf-shadow-black.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Unlock: </em>When you reach 6th level overall you may take the ability below.</p><p>Your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip ignores resistance to necrotic damage, and creatures that are immune to necrotic damage take half damage from it on a hit.</p><p>Additionally, over the course of a rest you can perform a ritual to merge a magical melee weapon with your shadow. At the end of the rest the weapon disappears and you attune to it, even if the item doesn&rsquo;t require attunement. While you have a weapon merged with your shadow, weapons created by your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip inherit all of the merged weapon&rsquo;s magical properties. If the weapon has charges or limited use abilities, track their expenditure as a single pool&mdash;summoning your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} multiple times does not grant extra uses of them. Creatures that closely inspect your shadow will notice that it appears to be holding the weapon while your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} isn&rsquo;t summoned or is banished.</p><p>A weapon merged with your shadow reappears a foot away from you when you die, your attunement to it ends, or you choose to merge a different weapon with your shadow. You can choose to end your attunement with a merged weapon over a rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "5Y5UKK5OB00AYMHG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Loyal Weapon", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/weapon-sword-skull-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip no longer requires concentration, and its duration is increased 8 to hours. The spell ends early if you cast it again. For the duration of the spell, you can banish and resummon the blade in place of sheathing or drawing a weapon.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "WXAA4GO3QQKD1H7M", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "One Foot in the Grave", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/graveyard-tombstone-night.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have resistance to necrotic damage. You also have advantage on Save Checks made to resist any effect that would reduce your maximum hit points.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "GJSBBBEWC3QHE19Y", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Reaper", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/weapons/sickles/scythe-curved-steel.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency with scythes. Whenever you cast the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip you can create a scythe with a damage die of 1d8 necrotic and the added trait <strong>Reach</strong>.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "VP1MJ4K008E0P5QE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Thanatophobia", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/skull-energy-light-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Each time you hit a creature with an attack using your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade}, you can spend 1 mana to attempt to instill fear in it. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom (Save) Check versus your spell save DC or become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened} of you until the end of its next turn. A creature that succeeds on its save is immune to this ability until the start of your next turn.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "H5SWPCUEGNVFEPPT", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tools of the Harvest", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/trades/farming-sickle-harvest-wheat.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip, and Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence is your spellcasting attribute for it.</p><p>If you already knew the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.QVIXYJFEAOXHF2SW]{Dread Blade} cantrip before selecting this Archetype or later learn it from another source, you instead gain proficiency with one of the following: daggers, sickles, shortswords, hatchets.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "5GKWWIQFXU0YBEWB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "The Best Defense", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/shield-block-bash-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>They say the best defense is a good offense. Well, who's to say your shield can't provide both.</p><p>You treat shields you wield as martial melee weapons with a damage die of 1d6 bludgeoning damage. Shields that lack the <b>Heavy</b> trait gain the trait <b>Thrown (20/60)</b>. Shields with the <b>Heavy</b> or <b>Two-Handed</b> trait gain an additional trait <b>Versatile (1d8)</b>.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "UN7U2EJY5GRE4EB6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Heads Up", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/instruments/megaphone.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you roll initiative and are not <b>Surprised</b>, you can quickly coordinate with one of your allies to prepare for the coming danger. After initiative has been rolled but before the first turn of combat, you can choose to immediately move adjacent to an allied creature that is reachable with half of your movement speed. If the chosen creature is ahead of you in the initiative order, move yourself to the spot immediately after it in the initiative order. Otherwise, move the creature to the spot immediately before you in the initiative order.</p><p>Subtract any movement used by this ability from the movement available to you on your first turn of combat. You can't use this ability on a creature that has already used or been the target of another copy of this ability in this combat.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "HS30FINEX9HB4RZE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Heroic Adrenaline", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/holy/barrier-shield-winged-cross.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Unlock: </em>When you reach 6th level overall and have the ability <i>Adrenaline</i> you may take the ability below.</p><p>Seeing others in peril stirs you to action and pushes you beyond your limits. Whenever you Size-Up an ally and learn that they are closest to \u00c2\u00bc Hit Points remaining or less, you can choose to regain an expended use of your <i>Adrenaline</i> ability. If you do, you can't use this ability on that same ally again until you finish a long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "N5DFPGT4NAZQ3RM9", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Retribution", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/hand/scale-balances-merchant-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Creatures within your weapon's reach provoke an attack of opportunity from you when they attack a creature other than you, unless the creature they are attacking also has this ability. If you hit with this attack of opportunity, your target's victim also gains 1d4 temporary hit points.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "G5GV21SNLQ4Q8K8C", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Bodyguard", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/equipment/shield/heater-crystal-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> A shield, with or without a weapon in your other hand.</p><hr><p>You step closer to your ward, holding your shield out so that it protects both of you. Surveying the field for threats they might not even see, you prepare yourself to do anything to keep the heat off of them.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Selfless Defense</b><ul><li>In addition to the normal methods, you can enter this stance at the end of a Self-Defense action or as a reaction to a creature ending its turn within 5 feet of you.</li></ul><b>Guardian</b><ul><li>One creature of your choice also gains the AC bonus of a single shield you are wielding while they are within 5 feet of you. A creature that is wielding a shield of its own does not gain this bonus.</li></ul><b>Got Your Back</b><ul><li>When an ally within 5 feet moves, you can use your Reaction to move with them up to your maximum movement speed.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>On Defense</b><ul><li>Creatures do not provoke Attacks of Opportunity from you when leaving your weapon range.</li></ul><b>Divided Protection</b><ul><li>You suffer a -1 penalty to your AC</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "L7C1Z21RZCX2NKTL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Decoy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/target-dummy.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> Not wielding a shield and not @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.YE63H7VLOHW7NFHO]{Invisible}. You can wield other weapons while in this stance as long as the requirements remain met.</p><hr><p>Squaring up your shoulders and standing boldly in clear view, you feign an opening in your defenses while confidently eyeing your foes, as if daring them to make the first strike. Getting through your enemy's armor will be trivial once your attitude has gotten under their skin.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Insult to Injury</b><ul><li>Your weapon and unarmed attacks deal an additional 1d4 psychic damage. The size of this damage die cannot be increased or decreased.</li></ul><b>Undaunted</b><ul><li>Creatures with the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.Y822OUCDEPAG0HS8]{Frenzied} condition do not add their Wisdom (Instinct) modifier to attack and damage rolls targeting you.</li></ul><b>Taunt</b><ul><li>As a minor action, you can attempt to goad a creature within 20 feet into a duel with you. They must make a Wisdom (Save) check of DC 8 + Your Presence Modifier + Your Proficiency Bonus. On a failure, they become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.Y822OUCDEPAG0HS8]{Frenzied} until the end of their next turn. The condition ends early if the creature can no longer see you or you move far enough away that the creature could not reach you without using the Dash action.</li><ul><li>If you activate this ability on a target after hitting them with at least one weapon attack in the same turn, the target suffers a -2 penalty to their Save check.</li></ul><li>Creatures @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.Y822OUCDEPAG0HS8]{Frenzied} by this ability:</li><ul><li>Always consider you the nearest target, even if other creatures are closer.</li><li>Can continue to concentrate on spells, but have disadvantage on checks to maintain concentration.</li><li>May still cast spells, but only if the spell involves making one or more attacks against you and no other creatures. Alternatively, the creature may target themself or an object with a spell if it would allow them to make an attack against you during the same turn it was cast.</li></ul></ul><b>That All You've Got?</b><ul><li>After you suffer bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, you can use your reaction to gain resistance to one of the listed damage types you just suffered for all subsequent attacks and effects, lasting until the start of your next turn.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Chip on Your Shoulder</b><ul><li>Your AC is reduced by 2.  If you are wearing Heavy armor, your AC is reduced by 3 instead.</li><li>Attacks of Opportunity have advantage against you.</li></ul><b>Inflated Ego</b><ul><li>Taking a Desperate Action causes you to immediately leave this stance before resolving the action.</li></ul><b>Obvious Target</b><ul><li>You automatically lose Dexterity (Stealth) contests against other creatures' Wisdom (Perception) or Awareness.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "TGJ46BXWJNNZTG8R", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Fortress", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/chess-rook-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> Heavy armor or a shield with the Heavy trait. You can wield other weapons while in this stance as long as the requirements remain met.</p><hr><p>You lean into the weight and heft of your armor or shield, carefully placing your feet and shoring up your balance to make any attempt to undermine you an uphill battle. You are a living wall of steel.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Impervious</b><ul><li>You can reduce Bludgeoning, Slashing, and Piercing damage you take by an amount equal to your proficiency bonus.</li></ul><b>Immovable Object</b><ul><li>You have advantage on checks made to avoid being moved or knocked prone.</li><li>Whenever you win a contested skill check to avoid being shoved, tripped, or grappled, you can immediately push your opponent 5 ft in any direction if they are no more than one size larger than you</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Weighed Down</b><ul><li>Your movement speed is halved.</li><li>You have disadvantage on Dexterity (save) checks.</li></ul><b>Obstructed Vision</b><ul><li>You have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight.</li></ul><b>Slow Setup</b><ul><li>You cannot switch into this stance as a non-action at the end of an attack.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "S8BIHKJPHEGR910P", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Rebound", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/light/beam-impact-deflect-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Requirement:</i> A Buckler or a bludgeoning weapon with the Thrown trait and no other weapons.</p><hr><p>You grip your throwing implement and wind back your arm, ready to hurl the mass towards an approaching foe. While blunt throwing weapons might not have the best aerodynamics, at this distance they pack enough punch to send attackers reeling back the way they came.</p><hr><u>Pros</u><p><b>Jumbo Discus</b><ul><li>Bucklers you wield gain the <b>Thrown (20/60)</b> trait.</li></ul><b>Go for Gold</b><ul><li>As an action, you can make a single thrown weapon attack that has advantage within its normal range and suffers no disadvantage from going beyond its normal range. Attacks that exceed the maximum range still miss.</li></ul><b>Rebound</b><ul><li>After making an attack with a thrown weapon, it bounces back towards you.</li><ul><li>If the attack hits, the weapon rebounds directly to you and you catch it.</li><li>If the attack misses, it bounces harmlessly and lands in a random space within 5 ft of you.</li></ul></ul><b>Confounding Blows</b><ul><li>When you hit a creature with your weapon, they have disadvantage on the first weapon attack they make before the end of their next turn.</li></ul><b>Bank Shot</b><ul><li>When you score a critical hit with a thrown weapon, you can choose to have it bounce towards another target instead of immediately returning. Make an attack with advantage against a different creature within the weapon's range from the current target. The weapon still returns after the attack chain ends, as long as there was no <b>Catastrophic Miss</b>.</li></ul></p><hr><u>Cons</u><p><b>Catastrophic Miss</b><ul><li>Upon critically failing a thrown weapon attack, the weapon does not return to you and instead flies 20ft past the target before hitting the ground.</li><li>Attacks beyond a weapon's maximum range also suffer a <b>Catastrophic Miss</b>.</li></ul><b>Conservation of Momentum</b><ul><li>The normal and maximum ranges of thrown weapons are halved.</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "stance"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "0FNB61M34QI8Q8AT", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fighting Stance: Gladiator", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/equipment/shield/heater-steel-sword-yellow-black.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn 1 fighting stance from the following list.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When you can choose a new Fighting Stance as part of leveling up, you can choose from one of these Fighting Stances as well.<br><br><u><i>Fighting Stance List: Defender</i></u><br>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.L7C1Z21RZCX2NKTL]{Bodyguard Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.S8BIHKJPHEGR910P]{Fortress Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.0FNB61M34QI8Q8AT]{Rebound Stance}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.TGJ46BXWJNNZTG8R]{Decoy Stance}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Must have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "5A7HOEBVANPTZD28", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Vigilant", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/watchtower-moonlit-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are always on alert, waiting for the other shoe to drop. You gain proficiency in Wisdom (Perception).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Fighter Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "IJ4DSNSC69UF86HZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Covetous Defiance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know to keep your friends close, your enemies closer, and your hoard closest of all. You gain a bonus to your maximum hit points based on the magic items you are attuned to at any given moment. The bonus for each item is determined by its rarity, as follows:</p><ul><li>Common: +1 maximum hit points.</li><li>Uncommon: +3 maximum hit points.</li><li>Rare: +5 maximum hit points.</li><li>Very Rare: +7 maximum hit points.</li><li>Legendary: +10 maximum hit points.</li><li>Artifact: +10 maximum hit points, and your maximum rest dice for Cleric increases by 1.</li></ul><p>Additionally, while you have all of your attunement slots filled you also gain a +1 bonus to all save checks.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Dragon Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "D1GJLP59RK0A613P", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Miracles of Draconic Transubstantiation", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-ice-breath-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Miracle</em> Adept ability.</p><p>In the moments when your faith comes into complete clarity, you find the will to temporarily transcend the limits of your physical form, reshaping it to embody one or more traits associated with dragons of your affinity.</p><p>The <strong>Transformation Miracles</strong> below are added to your pool of Miracle options. Each of these miracles lasts until you finish a long rest, and the number of Transformation Miracles you can have active at once cannot exceed your Proficiency Bonus. Some of the miracles can be activated a second time in order to upgrade its effects. Transformation Miracles upgraded in this way count as two active Transformation Miracles. If you activate a Transformation Miracle while you are at the limit, you must choose another active one to downgrade or end.</p><ul><li><strong>Armatura Draconis: </strong>Your skin is covered with dragon scales. Your AC can&rsquo;t be less than 16, regardless of what armor you&rsquo;re wearing, and you gain resistance to the damage type of your Elemental Affinity.&nbsp;<ul><li>Activating this miracle again grants immunity to the damage type of your Elemental Affinity.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Irae Draconis:</strong> You sprout a set of claws on each of your hands and a formidable dragon tail. The claws are natural weapons with a damage die of 1d6 slashing damage and have the Finesse and Light properties. The tail is a natural weapon with a damage die of 2d6 bludgeoning damage and Reach property, and while you are Medium or larger it also gains the Heavy property.<ul><li>Activating this Miracle again gives you the following ability: As a Minor Action, you can make a tail attack.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Potentia Draconis:</strong> Ridges emerge from your back as your stature bulks and lengthens. Your size increases by one category, unless you are already Large or bigger, and you have advantage on Strength checks. Your equipment grows with you so long as it is on your person.&nbsp;<ul><li>Activating this Miracle again grants an additional 5 feet of reach to all of your melee attacks and spells with a range of Touch.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Spiritus Draconis:</strong> Your head morphs to resemble that of a dragon, granting you the following ability: As an Action, you can spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die and exhale destructive power. Each creature in a 15 ft cone originating from you must succeed on a Dexterity (Save) check versus your Cleric Spell Save DC or take 3d6 damage in the damage type of your Elemental Affinity. On a successful save, a creature takes half damage.<ul><li>Activating this miracle again increases the ability&rsquo;s damage to 4d6 and the size of the cone to 20ft.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Volatus Draconis: </strong>You manifest a pair of dragon&rsquo;s wings, granting you a flying speed equal to your walking speed.&nbsp;<ul><li>Activating this Miracle again gives you the following ability: Until the miracle ends you can beat your wings as an Action and attempt to shove every creature that is within 5 feet of you. Creatures that fail are pushed an additional 5 feet and take 1d6 bludgeoning damage.</li></ul></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Dragon Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "DF3V1QA5MH23X8LZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Eikon: Dragon", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain an Eikonic Number as detailed in the <strong>Eikonic Numbers</strong> Cleric Starter Ability. However, instead of choosing an Eikonic number from one of the Potencies described in the table, you must pick a number from 13 through 17. This will be your <strong>Eikonic Number of the Dragon</strong>. This Eikonic Number otherwise functions the same as a Greater Potency number when you are assigning and activating Mantras (see the &ldquo;Eikonic Numbers&rdquo; Cleric Starter Ability for details).<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Seeing the elemental power of your affinity made manifest in the world serves as an additional source of conviction for your faith. Once per turn, when you roll at least one set of doubles on damage dice that match the type of your <strong>Elemental Affinity</strong>, you can activate your <strong>Eikonic Number of the Dragon</strong> as if you had rolled it.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Finally, assign two of the following Mantras to this new <strong>Eikonic Number of the Dragon</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Suffer No Insult:</strong> Until the end of your next turn, attackers that hit you with melee attacks suffer 1d4 damage of your Elemental Affinity&rsquo;s type.</li><li><strong>Mine, All Mine:</strong> Coins with a total gp value equal to your proficiency bonus appear in a container you&rsquo;re carrying.</li><li><strong>Inhale, Exhale:</strong> The next time you roll damage for an attack or spell before the end of your next turn, you can add your Wisdom modifier as extra damage of your Elemental Affinity&rsquo;s type.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "B1NJPCKFFLL7PFVJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elemental Affinity", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As part of becoming a cleric of the Dragon Dominion, you must choose one damage type to become your Elemental Affinity. Your choice of affinity will determine the damage type and spell options of other Dragon Dominion abilities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Choose one of the following to be your Elemental Affinity: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison.</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You can change your choice of affinity whenever you reach a growth level, replacing all abilities and spells granted by your old one. Once every 7 days, when you touch a living true dragon or permanent site of draconic worship, you can choose to change your affinity to the one most closely associated with the entity in question.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "UROYUWYQ5D1XOMRC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fearsome Presence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You exude the awe and power of the dragons. You gain proficiency in Presence (Intimidation) if you were not already proficient in it, and you can speak, read, and write Draconic.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "BP376DKTF70JKEHV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hoarded Blessings", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/currency/coin-engraved-tail-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Miracle</em> Adept ability.</p><p>Just as a dragon may amass their hoard over decades and centuries, so too have you learned to patiently collect wayward fragments of the powers that flow through you. These fragments are yours to keep and form your own personal reserve that grows and grows until its power cannot be contained.</p><p>You have a <strong>Spiritual Hoard</strong> number, an accumulating value that starts at 0. Each time you roll one or more @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{\u00f0\u0178\u2022\u00af Faith} Dice but do not trigger a Miracle, you may increase your Spiritual Hoard by the number rolled on one of the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{\u00f0\u0178\u2022\u00af Faith} Dice. If this causes the new total of your Spiritual Hoard to equal exceed 20, reset your Spiritual Hoard to 0 and immediately trigger a Miracle.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Dragon Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JKVO726WWVKAVE2W", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Purloined Essence", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a reaction to taking damage that matches your Elemental Affinity's type, you can spend your @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Dice to heal yourself for the total faith roll plus your Wisdom modifier. You can use this ability even if the initial damage was reduced to 0, for example as a result of resistance or immunity.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Dragon Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "4RLLUUNYF7O4NQJ6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dragon Dominion Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><i>Spells without compendium links set up are still undergoing approval</i></p><p>Clerics of the Dragon Dominion learn the following spells once able to cast spells of that level.&nbsp; These spells are always prepared and don&rsquo;t count against your prepared spell amount.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>If a dominion spell is not listed as a Cleric spell, it nonetheless counts as a Cleric spell for you.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><em>Dragon Dominion Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Dominion Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.DR1S6TA7ZZHXVKVY]{Menacing Visage},</em> and the additional spell of your Elemental Affinity.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.H12OZBL02CSFQX6L]{Dragon&rsquo;s Breath},</em> and the additional spell of your Elemental Affinity.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>Sprout Wings*,</em> and the additional spell of your Elemental Affinity.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.YL8USCAX1ZTDKOA1]{Shapeshift},</em> and the additional spell of your Elemental Affinity.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-5.IGNKJCNA0BXYD1OT]{Unnatural Recovery},</em> and the additional spell of your Elemental Affinity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Additional Spells by Affinity</em></p><style>table#affinity td{width:20%; max-width:20%; min-width:20%;} #affinity{min-width: 850px;}</style><table id='affinity'><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Acid Affinity</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Cold Affinity</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Fire Affinity</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Lightning Affinity</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Poison Affinity</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.MB7NWQ5H11LSIVV7]{Caustic Needle}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.KH6D03TEJYZNA62N]{Cold Snap}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Embers}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.0JWJ9J7A2AMSNDK0]{Jolt}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.3L7I8DH0G63AX9B1]{Create Miasma}</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-1.93IZ61HQGJ91795Y]{Brittle Beam}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.FBBZHRD9FHGJV2C4]{Hypothermia}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.LO6PLV28RA6CBCLU]{Burst Into Flames}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.37VLMG8DVH1QVCYM]{Charge Conduit}</em></p></td><td><p><em>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.N3BHT4QNPIDGVC6C]{Nocuous Bubble}</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-2.DV87F1MQUC5C59VW]{Corrosive Wash}</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-2.HVOF7QNI17K2O6C1]{Snowslide}</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-2.WR681XHI4K1RFFID]{Cauterize}</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-2.BNG42U9X3RWWFWXA]{Static Spark}</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.IGNXR8HBQZS1JVCY]{Ophidian Kiss}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>Astringent Bog*</em></p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.IJWDFSYAAI44S9JD]{Frigid Barrage}</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.7UWC00HNXCOL4GFI]{Fireball}</p></td><td><p><em>Wandering Storm*</em></p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.TA1E58P8XATOBEQH]{Virulent Outbreak}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p><em>Acidic Wave*</em></p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.H2RO4K8JLYTVNEXB]{Winter&rsquo;s Piercing Ray}</p></td><td><p><em>Burning Blood*</em></p></td><td><p><em>Pillars of Fulmination*</em></p></td><td><p><em>Neutralizing Venom*</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "PF2GG3QRNRTNOXYS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Barkhide", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your AC cannot be less than 16.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "V669TDIW4PJ80BHM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Botanical Creature", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your creature type is Fey, Beast, and Plant.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "GAIKNBY6N36Y6RO6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Branching Aspects", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Increase one attribute of your choice by 2. As a <em>Rest Action</em>, you can focus the magic in your body to slightly alter your form, allowing you to remove this bonus and reassign it to a different attribute.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.rest-actions.YCYYZ4X8PA6KSF26]{Alter Branching Aspect}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Q78C6Z5AKLUHOP26", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Deadly Dance", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your antlers gain the Finesse and Light traits. Any time your antlers deal damage with an attack that does not add your attribute modifier to the damage, you can choose to add half of your modifier to the damage.&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "W9RCBFZGJJ8246TI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Font of Mana", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Once per turn, when you are casting a spell you can choose to gain one level of the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhausted} condition in order to discount its mana cost by 4. On repeated uses, the mana discount is reduced by 1 for each time this ability has already been used since your last long rest. The&nbsp;@Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhausted} condition takes effect after the spell has been cast.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9695KHD24N6APCJQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Globetrotter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your walking speed increases by 10ft and you can ignore all non-magical difficult terrain.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AL7QGW1MM9CRUCCS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Herald Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your body transforms, becoming more sleek and lithe. Your body weight is reduced by a half, rendering you unnaturally light and quick on your hooves. Your hide becomes smooth with a texture like carved wood. Your crystal antlers grow thinner and the points flatten like thin blades.</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Dexterity and Wisdom both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Botanical Creature:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.GAIKNBY6N36Y6RO6]{Botanical Creature}</li><li><strong>Ossified Aptitude:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.FZ7JF27LF3N0UQ3T]{Ossified Aptitude}</li><li><strong>Globetrotter:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.AL7QGW1MM9CRUCCS]{Globetrotter}</li><li><strong>Deadly Dance:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.W9RCBFZGJJ8246TI]{Deadly Dance}</li><li><strong>Weathered Hide (replaces Tough Hide): </strong>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.8AKVHASX3I9XZMA8]{Weathered Hide}</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "JUXEYSN2P7EZD3C6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Knight Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your body transforms, becoming more stocky and muscular and increasing your body weight by one third. Your hide becomes sturdy and rough like bark, while still somehow retaining its ability to flex. Your crystal antlers broaden, thicken, and sprout a forest of lethally sharp points.</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Strength and Constitution both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Botanical Creature:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.GAIKNBY6N36Y6RO6]{Botanical Creature}</li><li><strong>Ossified Aptitude:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.FZ7JF27LF3N0UQ3T]{Ossified Aptitude}</li><li><strong>War Antlers:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.EO5MKICE044MS7PV]{War Antlers}</li><li><strong>Oaken Will:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.X7DK47I4S607ZZCR]{Oaken Will}</li><li><strong>Toughness:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.V14VJKEZYL6XOJLC]{Toughness}</li><li><strong>Barkhide:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.V669TDIW4PJ80BHM]{Barkhide}</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XQIU5OOB7L0LLU45", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mana Prism", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain a +1 magical bonus to weapon attack and damage rolls made with your antlers. Spells cast using your antlers as a somatic or material component gain a +1 bonus to spell attack rolls. You also gain the ability to attune and unattune to your own antlers as though they are a magic item. While you are attuned to your antlers, you gain a +1 bonus to the Save DC of spells you cast.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DVZYCXJ0A0X6A0NH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mind Over Matter", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can use your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence in place of Strength for attacks and checks made using your telekinesis, as well as for calculating how much weight you can lift and carry with your telekinesis.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Z96Q7Q8UM9BIS15N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mystic Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your body transforms, becoming more elegant and distinguished. Tufts of fur grow longer and take on the texture of hanging moss. The points of your antlers elongate upwards, forming a crown of varying-height points above your head like a crystal chandelier.</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Intelligence and Presence both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Botanical Creature:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.GAIKNBY6N36Y6RO6]{Botanical Creature}</li><li><strong>Ossified Aptitude:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.FZ7JF27LF3N0UQ3T]{Ossified Aptitude}</li><li><strong>Mind Over Matter:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.Z96Q7Q8UM9BIS15N]{Mind Over Matter}</li><li><strong>Magical Epiphany:</strong> You learn one cantrip and one spell of 3rd level or lower, regardless of class. Your spellcasting attribute for these spells is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence.</li><li><strong>Font of Mana:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.9695KHD24N6APCJQ]{Font of Mana}</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "R66ZDNJYPDYIN1NS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Oaken Will", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on checks to maintain concentration on your <strong>Innate Telekinesis</strong>.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "X7DK47I4S607ZZCR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ossified Aptitude", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Starting at 5th level, you can only use <strong>Sprouting Aptitude</strong> once per long rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FZ7JF27LF3N0UQ3T", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Rooted Aspects", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You do not lose the <strong>Branching Aspects</strong> ability of your branch race. However, changing which attribute the ability affects now takes a <em>Long Rest Action</em>.</p><p>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.rest-actions.DDSB3DNVPUQO2F8R]{Alter Rooted Aspect}</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "JLFL3Z4SQZCF0KJ4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Spectra Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>To some elkanths, this morph is viewed as a rejection of one&rsquo;s metamorphosis - the sign of an elkanth who cannot accept who they truly are. Others, however, believe the very nature of an elkanth is to contain multitudes of possibility within oneself. In their minds, to sacrifice this limitless ability to adapt for a single metamorphosis stands as the real betrayal of one&rsquo;s true self.</p><p>Unlike other morphs, there are no physical changes that accompany this choice. Instead, you have a sensation of being filled with untapped magical energy, and your crystal antlers shift in hue to become a kaleidoscope of prismatic colors.</p><ul><li><strong>Rooted Aspects.</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.JLFL3Z4SQZCF0KJ4]{Rooted Aspects}</li><li><strong>Mana Prism.</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.DVZYCXJ0A0X6A0NH]{Mana Prism}</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RW3NZGJT6FY8E162", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sprouting Aptitude", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you roll an attack or check but before learning whether you succeed or fail, you can choose to increase the total by an amount equal to your proficiency bonus. You can use this ability three times, regaining all expended uses on a short or long rest. You can&rsquo;t use this ability more than once on a single roll.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "IZYXPF83UQ61P6EH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Toughness", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have additional maximum hit points equal to your level.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "V14VJKEZYL6XOJLC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "War Antlers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The damage of your antlers increases to 1d12 and they gain the traits Heavy and Versatile (2d6). When you attack with your antlers, you can choose to treat the attack as either one-handed or two-handed for the purposes of traits and abilities.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EO5MKICE044MS7PV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Weathered Hide", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While you are not wearing armor, you have a base AC of 13 + Your Dexterity modifier.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "8AKVHASX3I9XZMA8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Crystal Antlers", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have crystal antlers which function as natural weapons that deal piercing damage equal to 1d8 plus your Strength modifier on a hit. You are proficient with your antlers, but they do not grant any extra attacks, actions, or minor actions on their own. Your antlers count as a magical weapon, as well as an arcane and druidic spellcasting focus. As long as your neck and head are not restrained, you can perform somatic components for spells by moving and turning your head.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "U6I2WOGZ7SJ06YAG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Innate Telekinesis", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have limited telekinetic abilities out to a range of 10 feet from you, which allows you to manipulate a single object you can see at a time. While manipulating an object in this way, you are considered to be holding it and it moves with you if it is free to do so. If you move more than 10ft away from an object that is unable to move with you, your hold on it ends. Switching from one object to another follows the normal rules for dropping, picking up, and interacting with objects. When you use your telekinesis, your antlers visibly glow and you can feel the lifted object&rsquo;s weight pushing down on you. Because of this, the maximum weight you can lift and drag with your telekinesis follows the normal rules based on your Strength, and anything you hold with it should be included when determining the total weight you are carrying.</p><p>As a minor action, you can begin to concentrate on your telekinesis as if it were a spell, allowing you to manipulate a single object as if using two hands until your concentration ends or you are no longer holding the object. If you roll a natural 1 on a Save Check to maintain concentration on an object, you involuntarily drop the object.</p><p>You can wield weapons using your telekinesis, but you are unable to effectively wield weapons with the Two-handed or Ammunition property unless you are concentrating on them. Attacks and checks made with the help of your telekinesis still use your Dexterity and Strength like a hand would, extending rather than replacing your own coordination and brawn. Targets that are at least partially inside the range of your telekinesis are within reach of your melee weapon attacks, and weapon traits that confer additional reach or range effectively extend this range by the same amount.</p><p>It is difficult for you to affect other creatures with your telekinesis. When targeting an unwilling creature or an item being worn or held by one, your telekinesis lets you attempt to Shove, Trip, Grapple, or pickpocket them with the normal action costs for these actions. You can use your telekinesis to drag, lift, or carry any creature that is either willing, @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9KB959MRZ0H4IT4C]{Unconscious}, or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.FGVFFYGPAFQGZ5RP]{Grappled} by you, as long as their weight does not exceed your normal capabilities.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "X90070WNOK4CT8IN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Light Mount", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can carry a single creature that is at least one size smaller than you on your back without reducing your movement speed. If this creature is wearing heavy armor, your movement speed is halved.<br />As long as the creature on your back is not encumbered, the weight of their body and equipment does not count against your carrying capacity. If they are encumbered, only the weight they are carrying in excess of their own carrying capacity is counted against yours. <br />Creatures can spend 5 feet of movement to get onto your back, so long as you are willing. Alternatively, you can spend a minor action to pull a willing creature that is at least one size smaller than you on or off of your back.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AVW92OOI16CTT0GO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Magical Creature", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your creature type is both Beast and Fey. You are not Humanoid.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1SSP874MS3JNF0FV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Quadruped", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are a quadrupedal creature, walking on four legs. You also have no arms to wield weapons, cast spells, control a mount, or otherwise interact with objects that require hands or arms.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YF5J81BX9N85CTSL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Tough Hide", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While you are not wearing armor, your base AC is 12 + your Dexterity modifier.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "S03TGQ7I743UOZQQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Aquatic Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can breathe both air and water. While you are in your <strong>Hybrid Form</strong> you have a base swim speed equal to your walking speed.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "LYYAWTVAUZ74GNO6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Avian Morp", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While you are in your <strong>Hybrid Form</strong>, you have wings with a base flying speed of 15ft. Any branch race traits that would alter your base flying speed instead modify this speed. To use this speed, you cannot be wearing medium or heavy armor.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "1UYXRB8EC8529C4N", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Echo Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your body transforms to take on minor aspects of your past life, for example, tufts of feathers for an avian race or webbed features for an aquatic race. The branch race you chose to represent a past life of yours in the <strong>Echoes of a Past Life</strong> trait begins to emerge as a unique morph.</p><ul><li><strong>Synthesis.</strong> At 5th level, you gain any Attribute Score adjustments, proficiencies, languages, and spells granted by your past life&rsquo;s branch race.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Ossified Echoes.</strong> At 5th level, you lose one trade proficiency of your choice. Additionally, choose two skills you are proficient with. Your proficiency bonus is halved for those two skills.</li><li><strong>Hybrid Form.</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.3F9RMIYWVEAYALGX]{Hybrid Form}</li><li><strong>Additional Traits.</strong> You gain an additional trait depending on the compatibility type of your past life&rsquo;s branch race.<ul><li><strong>Aquatic Morph:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.LYYAWTVAUZ74GNO6]{Aquatic Morph}</li><li><strong>Avian Morph:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.1UYXRB8EC8529C4N]{Avian Morp}</li><li><strong>Bestial Morph:</strong> Your Constitution and one other attribute of your choice both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Hominid Morph:</strong> One attribute of your choice increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Insectoid Morph:</strong> You receive one fewer +1 attribute increase during your level 5 growth level.</li><li><strong>Reptile Morph:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.2J2D85IU0LK75VTV]{Reptile Morph}</li></ul></li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YRLU5DY2C4QOIY0B", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hybrid Form", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Starting at 5th level, you can use your action to transform into a shape that is a hybrid of your current and past life in order to gain all of the remaining traits and abilities of your past life&rsquo;s branch race (i.e. those not already gained through <strong>Synthesis</strong>) including any forms of movement and special senses. If the branch race is normally of a size different from yours, you choose which of the two sizes to be for the duration. This transformation lasts until you fall <strong>unconscious</strong> or you choose to transform back as an action.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3F9RMIYWVEAYALGX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Reptile Morph", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>One attribute of your choice increases by 1. While you are in your <strong>Hybrid Form</strong>, the AC granted by your Tough Hide trait increases to 13 + your Dexterity modifier.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2J2D85IU0LK75VTV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ashen Drift", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/air/wind-stream-blue-gray.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While your familiar is within 60 feet of you, you can spend 2 mana to teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of it as a minor action.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "6Q8NPXGTPOTSP2KO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fuel the Flames", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-campfire-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Unlock: </em>When you reach 6th level overall you may take the ability below.</p><p>Whenever an ember created by your @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Ember} cantrip detonates, gain temporary hit points equal to the number rolled on the detonation damage die, not including any modifiers or bonuses.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "17T1JOINDUGBWTGS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Kindled Companion", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/projectile-smoke-swirl-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your familiar gains a bonus equal to your proficiency bonus to its AC, saving throws, attack rolls, and damage rolls of its attacks.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "RZWY2QVJ74LA8RZ6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Primordial Bond", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-eye.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-1.TT94JMKOUYP2WM96]{Cojoin Familiar} spell. Familiars you create with this spell gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>The familiar&rsquo;s attacks deal fire damage instead of the listed damage types.</li><li>The familiar is immune to fire damage.</li><li>The familiar&rsquo;s creature type is Elemental.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "06UDKKP6BQGSGKF8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Seeker's Knack", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-campfire-smoke.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You learn the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Ember} cantrip, and Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence is your spellcasting attribute for it.</p><p>If you already knew the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Ember} cantrip before selecting this Archetype or later learn it from another source, you instead gain proficiency with one of the following: sling, slingshot, or the Pathfinding Trade.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "1P73PV63XRZZ06AX", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Smoldering Quiver", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/fire/projectile-arrow-fire-orange-yellow.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency with one of the following: shortbow, longbow, light crossbow, heavy crossbow, repeating crossbow.</p><p>Whenever you cast the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Ember} cantrip, it creates 1d4 additional embers and you can choose to shape the embers into ammunition appropriate for any ranged weapon you are proficient with.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "3rd level overall and have at least one level each in a Martial and Spellcaster class", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "0XE5EBEOURNKXDWE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Amphibious", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/amphibians/frog-water-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can breathe air and water.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "activation": {"type": "", "cost": null, "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": ""}, "cover": null, "target": {"value": null, "width": null, "units": "", "type": ""}, "range": {"value": null, "long": null, "units": ""}, "uses": {"value": null, "max": "", "per": null, "recovery": ""}, "consume": {"type": "", "target": null, "amount": null}, "attribute": null, "actionType": "", "attackBonus": "", "chatFlavor": "", "critical": {"threshold": null, "damage": ""}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "formula": "", "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}, "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "FIAKA97FYXBI8RXA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Crushing Bite", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/lizard-mouth-glowing-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your powerful jaws function as a natural weapon that deals bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 plus your Strength modifier on a hit. You are proficient with your jaws, but they do not grant any extra attacks, actions, or minor actions on their own.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XTBTJVESG8QZXIDM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Deep Ocean Adaptation", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-bioluminous-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are adapted to the ocean's depths and do not suffer adverse effects of being in those environments.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Z8LMDPJW67U417SF", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elemental Equilibrium", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/social/trading-justice-scale-gold.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>After you cast a spell that deals cold or fire damage, you gain the condition <strong>Cold Attuned</strong> or <strong>Fire Attuned</strong> respectively, which are detailed below:</p><ul><li>Cold Attuned: When you cast a spell that deals cold damage, you and one target damaged by the spell before it ends suffer 1d4 cold damage. This condition ends after 1 minute or when you cast a spell that deals fire damage.</li><li><strong>Fire Attuned:</strong> When you cast a spell that deals fire damage, you and one target damaged by the spell before it ends suffer 1d4 fire damage. This condition ends after 1 minute or when you cast a spell that deals cold damage.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "614UPFMARNM1ROVC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Extremophile", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/skeleton-fish-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have resistance to fire and cold damage.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "ZSFV2WOU1HUP17KZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fearless", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/control/fear-fright-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have advantage on saving throws made to resist being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NG4N84ST7ES1J9IE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Heat Transfer", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/earth/lava-explosion-orange.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You know the @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.58I1UTE8ZV4CJ5W6]{Adherent Embers} and @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.KH6D03TEJYZNA62N]{Cold Snap} cantrips. Your spellcasting ability for them is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence, chosen when you select this race. The material component for Adherent Embers is replaced with volcanic rocks (consumed by the spell) which the spell heats to near molten.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "LSXJQMNO1E738IQC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Inject Venom", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/wounds/blood-cells-disease-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When you hit a creature with your bite, you can choose to deal an additional 2d4 poison damage. Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you finish a rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "PT5XC6EU86D58ODI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Moist Skin", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/amphibians/frog-water-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Whenever you spend an hour in an environment of extreme heat (such as a desert during daytime or terrain with exposed lava), you gain a level of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} if you don't already have any. In addition to the normal rules for resting, exhaustion imposed by this trait can be removed by fully submerging yourself in water.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "core"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "OQYT9KI73HD5VRJI", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Natural Regeneration", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/life/heart-shadow-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>If you lose an eye or appendage, it grows back over the course of 7 days. Whenever you spend a rest die to regain hit points, you can regain extra hit points on a low roll, as detailed below:</p><ul><li>D4 rest die: When you roll a 2 or lower on the die, add 2 to the total.</li><li>D6 rest die: When you roll a 3 or lower on the die, add 3 to the total.</li><li>D8 rest die: When you roll a 4 or lower on the die, add 4 to the total.</li><li>D10 rest die: When you roll a 5 or lower on the die, add 5 to the total.</li><li>D12 rest die: When you roll a 6 or lower on the die, add 6 to the total.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NZF69C583MKEQ0PB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Resist Toxins", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/toxins/cup-goblet-poisoned-spilled.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You have resistance to poison damage and advantage on saves made to avoid being @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened} or @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.SRRBLPRSJWGUR551]{Poisoned}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2PRN9S8X7YFBJP10", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Secrete Toxin", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/amphibians/bullfrog-glowing-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>When a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction to cause the attacker to take 1d4 points of poison damage. You can use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and regain all uses when you finish a rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "race", "subtype": "branch"}}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EZ51QFJQ8CC1P3GQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Eikon: Nature", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain a new Eikonic Number which serves as your <strong>Eikonic Number of Nature</strong> (see the &ldquo;Eikonic Numbers&rdquo; Cleric Starter Ability for details).</p><p>You also gain access to the following <strong>Mantras</strong>, which can only be assigned to your <strong>Eikonic Number of Nature</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Paths Less Traveled:</strong> Before the end of your next turn, you can move 10 feet once as a non-action on your turn. This does not subtract from your movement for the turn.</li><li><strong>The Land Heals in Time:</strong> You regain 2 hit points.</li><li><strong>Trust Your Instincts:</strong> Your Wisdom (Instinct) checks are increased by +5 for the next minute. You also immediately know which direction is North, and which direction is up.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "TNH2VR3UUITQYIWG", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Fruitful Faith", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/consumables/fruit/apple-red-tree-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As an action, you can spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die to conjure a blessed fruit. This fruit is a tiny object that persists until it is eaten or otherwise destroyed. Any creature that is holding one of these blessed fruits can use their minor action to eat the fruit and regain 2d6 hit points. Once per day, this ability can trigger a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.BREZS34CQ6PFBCNF]{Miracle} if you roll doubles on the dice. You can use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and regain all uses when you finish a long rest.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp; When you finish a long rest, any blessed fruits you conjured that have not been eaten rapidly decay into compost. They are destroyed and you regain a @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die for each.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Natural Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "P97169W6CB1L94C4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Nature Provides", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency with either the Botany, Fishing, or Pathfinding Trade.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "7YFK8JVWZMT9FTKS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Seasons of Faith", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/nature/plant-sproud-hands-dirt-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The seasons serve as a powerful example of how life can endure and even thrive amid changing circumstances, a lesson you choose to emulate with your faith.<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You gain the following unassigned Mantras associated with your <strong>Eikonic Number of Nature</strong>, and you may replace one of your assigned Mantras with one of these new ones. Each time you activate <strong>Faith Abides</strong>, you can choose one of these Mantras to also occur. The Mantras are:</p><ul><li><strong>Spring&rsquo;s Sprawl:</strong> Thorny bushes with flowers appear in a 10ft square centered on a point you can see within 30ft of you. Any creature that enters a space with a thorn bush takes 1d4 piercing damage. Thorns in a space are destroyed automatically when attacked directly or if the space is subjected to any fire damage.</li><li><strong>Summer&rsquo;s Glow:</strong> A swarm of fireflies appear around you and fly any distance up to 30ft in a direction of your choosing. The fireflies shed dim light in a 5ft radius and remain in place once they reach their destination or can&rsquo;t move any further. The fireflies scatter after 1 minute.</li><li><strong>Autumn&rsquo;s Canvas:</strong> A 5ft-tall juvenile tree adorned with autumn leaves emerges in an unoccupied space you can see within 30ft of you. Creatures can move through the tree&rsquo;s space normally. The tree is too weak to support anything larger than a Tiny creature attempting to climb it, but it can provide Half Cover to Medium or smaller creatures obscured by it. At the end of your next turn, all of the leaves fall from the tree and it is no longer suitable for use as cover.</li><li><strong>Winter&rsquo;s Blanket: </strong>A 15ft square within 30ft of you is blanketed with snow and becomes difficult terrain. The snow melts at the end of your next turn or when its space is subjected to any fire damage.</li></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Natural Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "ES1J6R9RFQJ33HVU", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Natural Dominion Spells", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Clerics of the Natural Dominion learn the following spells when able to cast Cleric spells of the same spell level.&nbsp; These spells are always prepared and don&rsquo;t count against your prepared spell amount.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Dominion spells are considered Cleric spells when learned this way.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Natural Dominion Spells</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Able to Cast</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-1.4952YYFV3OJ53IKQ]{Fists of Stone}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.spells-level-1.1BWH53RXWUBCUZI6]{Camouflage}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.IGNXR8HBQZS1JVCY]{Ophidian Kiss}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.UEGGABQ79I8A8CG5]{Twister}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>Astringent Bog, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-3.W7NSYVVHKA2Q2MBJ]{Geyser}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>@Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.YL8USCAX1ZTDKOA1]{Shapeshift}, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.2C1AA6FEY5D1JHV5]{Trapdoor Sinkhole}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th Level Cleric Spells</p></td><td><p>Safe Arbor*, @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-4.H2RO4K8JLYTVNEXB]{Winter's Piercing Ray}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "5APSGJ7C1CI9DA0F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Miracle: Spirit Animal", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/spirit-deer-herd-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><em>Requirement: </em>The <em>Miracle</em> Adept ability.</p><p>When you learn this ability, the following Miracle is added to your list of options available when a Miracle is triggered.<ul><li><b>Custodia Naturalis:</b> You summon a Spirit Animal in an unoccupied space within 15 feet of you, choosing its form to be a Bear, Eagle, Panther, or Wolf. The statistics for the creature are detailed later in this ability. The Spirit Animal acts immediately after your turns in combat and follows your commands. It lasts until you complete a long rest or it drops to 0 hit points. If you activate this miracle while you already have a Spirit Animal summoned, you can replace its form with another from the list, restore all of its hit points, and make it reappear in an unoccupied space within 15 feet of you.</li></ul></p><br><br><h3>Spirit Animal</h3><p>Medium Celestial (Small Celestial in Eagle Form)</p><p>AC 14</p><p>Hit Points 5 + 5 times your Cleric Level</p><p>Speed 40ft, climb 30ft</p><table><tbody><tr><td><p>STR</p></td><td><p>DEX</p></td><td><p>CON</p></td><td><p>INT</p></td><td><p>WIS</p></td><td><p>PRE</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>16 (+3)</p></td><td><p>16 (+3)</p></td><td><p>16 (+3)</p></td><td><p>3 (-4)</p></td><td><p>14 (+2)</p></td><td><p>7 (-2)</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Skills: Instinct +4, Perception +4, Stealth + 5</p><p>Awareness: 14</p><p>Challenge: &ndash;-</p><p><strong>Eagle Form.</strong> In Eagle Form, the Spirit Animal loses its climbing speed and half of its move speed, and gains a flying speed of 60 ft.</p><p><strong>Bear Form.</strong> In Bear Form, the Spirit Animal has resistance to bludgeoning, slashing, and piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Wolf Form.</strong> In Wolf Form, the Spirit Animal has advantage on attacks if one or more of its allies are within 5 feet of the target.</p><p><strong>Panther Form.</strong> In Panther Form, the Spirit Animal can hide as a minor action.</p><p><strong>Actions</strong></p><p><strong>Claws.</strong> Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft, one target. Hit: Deal 1d4+3 slashing damage.</p><p><strong>Bite.</strong> Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft, one target. Hit: Deal 1d8+3 piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Multiattack. </strong>The Spirit Animal makes one attack with its Bite and one with its Claws.</p><p><strong>Pounce (Panther Form only).</strong> The Spirit Animal makes one attack with its bite. If it was hidden from its target, the attack deals an additional 2d8 damage on a hit.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Natural Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "1YD5VVREY3QRIR5L", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Squeak Easy", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/creatures/mammals/rabbit-movement-glowing-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can conduct a 1 minute long ritual to attune yourself to the local wildlife of an area, granting you the ability to converse with the nearby fauna. At the end of the ritual, one or more nearby Beasts (any area with vegetation will usually have at least one Tiny Beast such as a mouse, squirrel, or bird) approaches you and you may ask it questions about the local area. Any beasts you speak to as part of the ritual are considered @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by you for the duration. The creatures have a basic understanding of all of the following within a 1 mile radius: persistent hazards, dangerous monsters, routine humanoid activity, and unusual events that have occurred within the last 10 days. The creatures are not able to identify specific people, kinds of monsters, or iconography but they can provide simple, surface-level descriptions such as \"a huge flying lizard\" for a dragon or \"a big hairy person with horns and a red cloak\" for a minotaur cultist.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The ritual's effects last until you decide to end them, you move more than 30 feet from the spot where you began it, or 1 hour has passed. If one or more of the beasts affected by the ritual are harmed by you or your allies, the effects immediately end and you lose 1 @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.65D4NMYRBMKHW59K]{&#x1F56F; Faith} Die.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Natural Dominion", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "J1I3ZN58X2VSQ2YJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wisdom of the Wilderness", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You gain proficiency in Intelligence (Nature) if you were not already proficient in it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "starter"}, "requirements": "", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "JWVFZMLVKQEYJGVO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Blood-Soaked Hands", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/toxins/poison-bottle-open-blood-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your words and actions can stir the cruelest ambitions lurking in the hearts of your fellow incorrigibles. Whenever you <b>Commit to the Bit</b>, any creatures hit by the assisted creature's weapon attacks before the end of its next turn gains the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding} condition.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "X7GBQG8CSADQYOZH", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Commiseration", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You are obsessed with the schemes and passions which rule the mind of man. You gain proficiency in Wisdom (Insight).</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "M7ONN7XQ5CD8VK24", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Star-Crossed Duel", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-pink.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You can sense when it's time for a duel to take a fatal turn. Whenever a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{&#x1F9FF; Villainized} creature you can see within 60ft of you is hit with a weapon attack by a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{&#x1F981; Lionized} creature, you can use your reaction to spend 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point and cause the creature to suffer additional damage equal to your Presence modifier plus two rolls of the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{&#x1F9FF; Villainized} bonus die.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you activate this ability as a desperate action, it only requires the attacker to be @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.ZOBZ8V2YME5YOYZR]{&#x1F981; Lionized} or the target to be @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.conditions.WHN3T2G6R8HUKOQX]{&#x1F9FF; Villainized}, not both, and the bonus damage increases by an additional die.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "PDP9D8MMKDY2DZSL", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "The Bell Tolls", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/tools/instruments/bell-brass-brown.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The ghastly visage of death is but a grim reminder of the fallibility of our mortal flesh. As a reaction to the death of a creature you can see, you can single out another creature within 20ft of it to instill terror into. If the target can hear you, it must succeed on a Wisdom (Save) check versus your spell save DC or become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened} by the sight of the corpse until the end of its next turn. Succeed or fail, the target can't be affected by this ability again until 24 hours have passed.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "AI1FILJPEB8JVZ6L", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Theme: Mortality", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/gallows-hanged-humanoid.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Your art is fueled by the pathos that comes with seeing even the mightiest champions brought low by doubt and ill fate. Whenever a creature you can see within 60ft of you is hit by a natural 20 on an attack roll, rolls a natural 1 on a save check, or when one of your allies fails a death throw, gain 1 @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You can only benefit from one Theme ability at a time. If you have multiple Theme abilities, you can change which one is active when you finish a short or long rest and any time you spend a @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZVH8L715PTWTQLSE]{&#x2728; Flair} point on an ability.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "given"}, "requirements": "Have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "4A26NHYUBD8OXCX5", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Untimely Remorse", "type": "ability", "img": "icons/magic/death/grave-tombstone-glow-teal.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>As a reaction to one of your allies being reduced to 0 hit points or killed, you can force the creature responsible to make a Wisdom (Save) Check versus your spell save DC. On a failure, the creature is overcome with grief, surprise, or some other unexpected emotion, and is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.3CQC3JEY2C3Y721F]{Incapacitated} until the start of its next turn.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If your ally was killed instantly, the creature has disadvantage on the save.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "type": {"value": "class", "subtype": "subclass"}, "requirements": "Must have the Bard Starter Abilities", "recharge": {"value": null, "charged": false}}, "folder": null, "_id": "9KHMDNUC50478I0D", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
